      "description": "Watch Middlesbrough vs West Brom highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The Championship encounter between Middlesbrough and West Bromwich Albion promised to be a high-stakes tactical battle as both sides looked to gain momentum early in the season. Fans packed the stadium, anticipating a fierce contest between two historic clubs with promotion aspirations. A Tight Tactical Opening The match, held on 2026-08-29 , began with both teams displaying defensive discipline. Neither side was willing to commit too many men forward in the early stages, leading to a cagey affair in the midfield. West Brom were forced into an early tactical adjustment in the 40th minute when Jeremy Sarmiento was replaced by Max Arfsten . Despite several half-chances and tactical skirmishes, the first half ended goalless, leaving everything to play for in the second period. Explosive Second Half and Lankshear’s Brilliance Everything changed immediately after the restart. In the 48th minute, Will Lankshear broke the deadlock with a clinical finish to give West Brom the lead. The visitors didn't stop there; in the 65th minute, Jimmy-Jay Morgan doubled the advantage, expertly converting an assist from Isaac Price . The momentum was firmly with the Baggies, and Will Lankshear capitalized again in the 73rd minute, netting his second goal of the game to put the visitors three goals up and silence the home crowd. Late Drama and Final Whistle Middlesbrough refused to go down without a fight and introduced Alfie Jones and Kyle Joseph to spark a comeback. Their persistence paid off in the 87th minute when Alfie Jones found the back of the net, assisted by the experienced Luke Ayling . However, it proved to be too little, too late for the hosts. West Bromwich Albion managed the final minutes professionally, including six minutes of stoppage time, to secure a vital three points on the road."
